course: dictionary
lesson: 6336
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, so look at the sentence to find the one the writer means. «Mount Everest is the highest mountain above sea level at 8,849 metres.» Here mountain means a very high hill with steep sides.
explain: Mountain can also mean a very large amount of something. «Her homework was a mountain of sums and spellings.» Nobody is climbing anything here. The sentence tells you there was a huge pile of work, so a mountain of means a very large amount.
explain: Mountainous is a describing word, made from mountain with -ous at the end, like famous or dangerous. A mountainous land is a land with many mountains in it. When you meet a new word, ask: is it a thing, an action, or a describing word? Then check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence.
fact: A mountain is a very high hill with steep sides, usually higher than about 600 metres.
fact: A mountain of homework means a very large pile or amount of homework.
fact: Mount Everest, on the border of Nepal and China, is the highest mountain above sea level, at 8,849 metres.
fact: Mountains are colder higher up, and the weather can change fast, so tell someone your route and wear proper clothes.
fact: Mountain ranges include the Rockies (USA and Canada), the Southern Alps (New Zealand), and the Great Dividing Range (Australia).
exercise: «Mount Everest is the highest mountain above sea level.» What is a mountain? | *A very high hill with steep sides | A small, flat field by a river | A road that winds through a town | A deep, wide lake
exercise: «Her homework was a mountain of sums and spellings.» What does mountain of mean here? | A small, neat pile | A kind of bike | A tall, steep hill | *A very large amount
exercise: Which word describes a land full of mountains? | mountain bike | molehill | mountain range | *mountainous
test: Jay says «make a mountain out of a molehill» means digging holes in a garden. What does it really mean? | *To make a small problem seem huge | To climb a hill very quickly | To dig holes in a garden
test: «Most stories climb a story mountain: an opening, a build-up, a problem, a resolution, and an ending.» What is a story mountain? | *A way of showing the shape of a story, from opening to ending | A real mountain in a book | A list of mountains with names | A map of hills
exam: In «mountains of water ice» on Pluto, which meaning of mountain fits best? | A small hill of snow | A very large amount of ice | A ride on a bike | *Very high, peaks rising up from the surface
